<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $67.5 mln Oct 11.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $67.5 mln Oct 11.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $67.5 million surplus on October 11 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON OCTOBER 11</p>
<p>Exports: $122.8 million</p>
<p>Imports: $148 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $365.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $272.4 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $67.5 million</p>
<p>OCTOBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.450 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.246 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.267 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.446 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.025 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
